  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Hypersexualization",
  "description": "The meme uses the phrase 'hold my hookah pipe!' in conjunction with the image of a Black woman discussing interracial marriage, implying that she is being 'held' or controlled by a male perspective. This is a form of hypersexualization, as it reduces her to an object of male desire or control, reinforcing the stereotype that Black women are sexually available or must be 'held' by men. This stereotype is part of a broader pattern of racialized sexual objectification of Black women.",
